-- title:
--   Adapted primitive element at a place of a curve
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq E \subseteq F$ be a tower of fields (with $F$ an $E$-algebra, $E$ and $F$ being $K$-algebras compatibly), with $K$ infinite and $F/E$ finite and separable, and let $w$ be a place of $F$ over $K$, i.e. a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}_w$ of $F$ that contains the image of $K$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring. Write $w.\mathrm{restrict}\,E$ for the place of $E$ over $K$ whose valuation subring is the preimage of $\mathcal{O}_w$ under $E \to F$, and for a place $v$ let $v.\mathrm{ord}$ be the associated normalised integer valuation, namely minus the $\mathrm{WithZero}$-logarithm of the adic valuation attached to the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_v$. The assertion is that there exist $\theta \in F$ and $c \in K$ such that: $\theta$ is integral over the valuation ring of $w.\mathrm{restrict}\,E$; the intermediate field $E(\theta)$ generated by $\theta$ is all of $F$; $w.\mathrm{ord}(\theta - c) = 1$, so that $\theta - c$ is a uniformiser at $w$; and $w'.\mathrm{ord}(\theta - c) = 0$ for every place $w'$ of $F$ over $K$ with $w'.\mathrm{restrict}\,E = w.\mathrm{restrict}\,E$ and $w' \neq w$.
--
--   This is the standard construction of a primitive element of $F/E$ adapted to a place $w$: integral over the place below, generating $F$, and with $\theta - c$ a uniformiser at $w$ and a unit at the other places of $F$ in the same fibre. It is used in the local comparison of differentials and the different along a fibre, and feeds into [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_smul_D_eq_smul_dCoord_of_forall_isIntegral_trace_mul_eq_aeval`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_smul_D_eq_smul_dCoord_of_forall_isIntegral_trace_mul_eq_aeval).
